Z||000013||TRiAD||12-19-2001||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>...if the record companies would stop making these rediculous profits on CDs, maybe more people would buy them and less people would copy them. The artist only gets a few dimes per CD, the shop gets a few dollars, and the rest is for the record company.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>BINGO! <P>It costs LESS THAN $.10 to make each copy a major CD release, including EVERYTHING except the artist's investment in studio time and equipment, training, etc. Most places still charge $15-17 for them. The artist is LUCKY if they get an equal amount to the original $.10 it cost to produce. Now, there are instances where the record co pays for the recording time, and this saves <I>established</I> artists thousands, but the new guys have it tough. <P>One reassuring thing, there are a growing number of "independantly produced and promoted" projects coming out, and more and more "CD manufacturing" companies (Like Oasis, for example) working WITH underground artists to produce and distribute their works (through BarnesandNoble.com, Amazon.com, etc) <I>without</I> the need for the "big record companies". <P>When it's time to cut 1000+ copies of my project, they're getting my business, and anyone can buy it through Barnes and Noble. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||TRiAD||12-19-2001||11:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>Last I knew you were allowed to make one backup of ANY media(cd, vhs, tape, even beta  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>True. You're allowed to legally allowed to make backups of materials you've paid for. <BR>You may have just hit on LEGAl grounds to sue Universal in a class actions suit.<P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>...my disclaimer: sod off, I dont care if you dont like my opinion, I dont wanna hear your comments on them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sod off yourself. Ray got flack for always contradicting himself and personally engaging in actions he condems others for. As far as I know, you haven't done that, so you weren't going to GET any comments on your opinions. <P>Nothing like baiting for an argument. <P>||||reg||1
